-- title:
--   Regular special fibre at ordinary ∞-branch points, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'\ge 1$ be an integer not divisible by $q$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ for which some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ satisfies $\iota(\zeta)=\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L(\!(X)\!)$ over $L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, i.e. $K=$ `laurentBaseChange L (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M'))`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, perfect residue field, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and uniformiser $\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal; $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with image in $L(\!(X)\!)$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $X^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ` of the modular invariant, and write $\mathfrak{X}=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`, the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$ along their common overring chart. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f\cdot y=x$ in $L(\!(X)\!)$ after applying $A\to L$ coefficientwise. Let $z\in\mathfrak{X}$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}$ obtained by pulling back $\varpi$ along the structural morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$; assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$. Assume $z$ is the image under the chart immersion `ιFin` of a point $y$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart whose prime is maximal, that for some ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with kernel that maximal ideal the value $\varphi(j)$ does not lie in `ssJSet q`$\,\Omega$ — the set of $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$ — and that every element of the finite chart algebra whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in that maximal ideal. Then the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the regularity of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X(\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M'))$ at those closed points of the finite $j$-chart that lie on the branch cut out by the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$ and have ordinary $j$-invariant, in the excluded small case $q=2$ (the companion result covers $q\ge 5$); the conclusion has the same shape as in that case, with the hypothesis $q=2$ replacing the lower bound on $q$. It feeds the construction of open neighbourhoods on which the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ is smooth and the regularity statement at good points of the integral model.
